title: Start
---
Hello traveler, find the shop keeper - he's a cool guy

<<declare $quest = "find shopkeeper">>

===

title: TalkToShopKeeper
---
<<if $quest == "find shopkeeper">>
  Buenos Dias Nacho Brochacho, I need money please gimmie a coin.
  <<set $quest to "find coin">>
<<elseif $quest == "find coin">>
  Ay im so poor     
  <<if has_item("Player", "shiny")>>
     Dios Mio you have a coin, thx gng.
  <<else>>
     need me some coin, some scrach, some cheddar
  <<endif>>  
<<endif>>
===

title: MissionStart
---
<<set $quest to "Explore station">>
Alright, finally made it in here.
Can't beleive they assigned me to a station so far this close to the holidays. 
Heh, really squeezing the most labour they can possibly get outta me...
Oh well, Jobs a job, not like theres anyone else to work for in the star system. Gotta eat somehow.
But why here? This place is a Ghost town. I couldn't even find records on when it was abbandoned?
Whatever, I gotta find a terminal and establish a connection with homebase. 
===

title: LockedDoor
---
Huh, doors still locked.
It must have a dual lock mechanism, a second button must be here somewhere
good thing I brought a flashlight -f-
<<set $quest to "Find a terminal">>
===

title: meetScrubs
---
Huh? They sent another? About time!
You've got no idea how long I've just spent trying to repair this damn terminal. 
Man I'm so hungry, do they really expect us to survive through operations with such small rations? 
Anyways, I'm Scrubs, I assume you're here for the same reason I am
... which we dont know, YET.
With this terminal working now we should be able to get our instructions from homebase
Let's get this done quick, this place gives me the creeps. 
I mean seriously, why send an expedition this close to a black hole? I highly doubt an abandoned mining rigs gonna have anything THAT valuable.  
<<if $quest == "Find a terminal">>
 <<set $quest to "Contact HQ">>
<<endif>>
===

title: contactHQ
---
<<if $quest == "Find a terminal">>
 I should prabably adresst this dude first...
<<endif>>
<<if $quest == "Contact HQ">>
  <color=green>INITIATING POST</color>
  <color=green>POST SUCESSFULL</color>
  <color=green>BOOTING STATION OS</color> 
  <color=green>...</color>
  <color=green>...</color>
  <color=green>WELCOME</color>
  <color=green>AQUILA CORP NEUROCHIP DETECTED - EXTRACTOR ID 7702eI</color>
  <color=green>REQUEST CURRENT DIRECTIVES?</color>
  well, yeah
  <color=green>PING SENT</color>
  <color=green>...</color>
  <color=green>...</color>
  <color=green>DIRECTIVES RECEIVED</color>
  <color=green>GAIN ACCESS TO STATION CENTRAL HUB AND AWAIT FURTHER INSTRUCTIONS</color> 
  <color=green>END MESSAGE</color>
  *Scrubs looks over to you*
  Huh, guess thats that
  why'd the corp wanna restore this place? it's a junkyard
  they can't possibly want to recomission it, especially with how close that black hole it is
  unless this is another way of laying off without having to send severance packages
  I get it, neurmail's expensive these days, heheh 
  Anyways, we'll need to activate the backup power if we wanna get to the main hub.
  could you take one for the team and re activate the station batteries? I'm like, really beat from this terminall
  this button behind me should unlock the baterry room down the hall
  according to the station doccumentation there are 3 ovveride buttons linked to the batteries
  no schematics though, so you'll have to find them yourself. Sorry bro.
  If you do get the doors to open then just head to the hub without me, i'll have to finnish up some wiring whilst i'm still down here
  <<walk_to "NPC" "WalkToServerEvent">>
  <<set $quest to "Reactivate power">>
<<endif>>

===

title: level1Note
---
you find an old paper note that reads; 
To whoever keeps downloading unauthorised homebrews to the projector for films PLEASE STOP
tamering with equipment without permission will garuantee a VERY DEEP pay cut
You know Aquilla doesn't stand for employees stepping out of line so from the bottmom of my heart
PLease stop, or else we'll all be eating the cheap and bland nutripaste for the next dozen cycles
Synth meats already enough of a delecacy...
===




// level 2

title: level2Start
---
<<set $quest to "Find a terminal and run diagnostics">>
...
What the hell was that!?
I better find a terminal and try to evaluate the actual health of this station
===

title: terminalDiagnostics
---
<color=green>ASSESSING SYSTEMS</color>
<color=green>SYSTEMS ONLINE</color>
<color=green>ASSESSING POWER LEVELS </color>
<color=green>MAIN GENERATORS ONLINE - HEALTH FUNCTIONAL</color> 
<color=green>ASSESSING STEERING CONTROLS</color>
<color=green>WARNING! FACILITY THRUSTER OFFLINE - SCANS SHOW HEAVY PHYSICAL DAMAGE</color> 
<color=green>HULL INTEGRIDY MOMENTARILY STABLE, IT IS ADVISED TO FOLLOW SAFTEY PROTOCOLS AND REPAIR DAMAGE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE</color>
<color=green>...</color>
damn, something must have malthfunctioned
I mean, I know this place is old, but even then its strange to see something break out of the blue just like that
I gotta on with HQ 
<color=green>TERMINAL COMMAND ; SEND_PING<NEURICHIP.LOCAL_BASE></color>
<color=green>PING SENT</color>
<color=green>...</color>
<color=green>DIRECTIVES RECEIVED</color>
<color=green>LOCATE AND RETREIVE STATION CORE</color>
<color=green>YOU MUST ENSURE THAT ACCESS TO CORE DOES NOT FALL IN ANY PERSONS OUTSIDE AQUILLA CORP</color>
<color=green>FALIURE TO DO SO WILL RESULT IN IMMEDIATE DEMOTION OF EMPLOYEE POSITION</color>
<color=green>END</color>
Damn, I gotta get to that core quick
if anything happens to it, I bet both me and that guy will become street beggars in a week tops
Speaking of which, I should find him
<<set $quest to "Find Co-worker Scrubs">>
===

title: talkToScrubs
---
<<if $quest == "Find Co-worker Scrubs">>
 Im not seeing things am I?
 A thruster down, this close to a black hole
 just my luck
 Hey, you saw the directives too right? we gotta get movin quick 
 Ive got good news and bad news
 The good news is ive scanned most of this place, so I know where everything is
 The bad news is that this whole tech graveyard is running on an old codebase, so we cant replicate any of the access cards with the software on our chips
 theres a master computer in the offices with red access for the core room, but that place is locked down too
 luckily, if this old employee records sheet that I found is true, there should be an overseer's desk somewhere in storage, the door behind you 
 go find it quick, it should have a keycard for the offices
 ill have to stay behind and reroute some power, if too much voltage gets through those faulty thrusters they may turn on without us being able to control them!
 we gota move quick, who knows what can kill us here... or who
 We are in the systems edge after all, you know, far from Aquilla's eyes
 if those stories of corp hating psychos are true, they'd be taking place in somewhere like here... 
 <<set $quest to "Obtain Office Access">>
<<elseif $quest == "inform scrubs">>
 I just had to mention it DIDN'T I?
 before you ask yeah, I heard that too
 we can't give up the core, what they'll make of us if we lose it... I have people to feed
 they're bluffing though, they have to be
 they cant damage the station any more or else they risk turning it into that black hole's breakfast, including the core
 as long as the external hatches stay locked we should be safe, ill keep track of cam footage
 Got the card? good, now get the red access and go straight to the core, no time to lose now
 <<set $quest to "Get Core Room Access">>
<<elseif $quest == "Get Core Room Access">>
 can't hold them off for long, get that core
<<elseif $quest == "Return to Co-Worker scrubs">>
 Got the core? Nice!
 I managed to hack that rouge ship, their tracking systems should be down
 We can walk through the exit behind me, get in a shuttle and slip away 
 It's almost over, we can got home from this mission just in time to do another one, ahah
 but seriously, lets get moving. they're still trying to get in. 
 <<set $quest to "Move to the exit">>
<<endif>>
===

title: keycardOne
---
that should be the card
huh? im getting a nerocom request from somewhere out the station
could be another extractor, let me patch them in
<color=red>Whatever you came for, it's not worth what you'll get out of it</color>
<color=red>the core, forget about it and no one gets hurt</color>
<color=red>we have more of what made those thrusters melt, please, don't play the hero</color>
<color=red>leave while you can</color>
oh god, ive gotta get to Scrubs
<<set $quest to "inform scrubs">>
===


title: transmition
---
RED ACCESS TRANSFERED
NOTE ; ANY UNAUTHERISED TAMPERING WITH CORE WILL LEAD TO IMMEDIATE TERMINATION
Ok, thats done
<color=red>you're an extractor arent you?</color>
<color=red>you have to be, not like they'd send someone of "value" all the way out here</color>
<color=red>Ive met others like you, even befriended some</color>
<color=red>we're not so different you know, except for the strings around your wrists, decided to take mine off years ago </color>
<color=red>let me guess, they've started straight up chucking faliures to the strees by now </color>
<color=red>was only a matter of time till they could afford it</color>
<color=red>your like a drone, extractor</color>
<color=red>a disposable oversight to do the dirty work </color>
<color=red>to think a battery can dictate your livleyhood </color>
<color=red>step out of line and... poof</color>
<color=red>you get consumed in a sea of misery</color>
<color=red>a sea only inches far enough for you to stay dry, ever lastingly waiting for you to slip up</color>
...
<color=red>damn, that was quite deep, never knew I was such a phillosipher</color>
<color=red>you're smart to lock yourself in, but it won't keep me out forever </color>
<color=red>i'm getting that core. </color>

===
title: transmition2
---
Got the Core!
<color=red>they took my neurochip, yknow?</color>
<color=red>my identity, money, contacts all lost</color>
<color=red>or I "returned company property" as they would have liked to say it </color>
<color=red>quite a tame description, considering I wasn't necesarilly lying in that surgical chair out of my own volition</color>
<color=red>all cause of a split second decision to prioratize life over property </color>
<color=red>yeah yeah, I'm being vauge and all but does it matter WHY I got cut loose? </color>
<color=red>what matters is how they do it</color>
<color=red>what matters is the mold they want you to fit into </color>
<color=red>a loyal husk, blindly following "Directives"</color>
<color=red>the perfect servant is one completly relient to you</color>
<color=red>eating your food, living in your home, carrying your name</color>
<color=red>one wrong step and you lose that name</color>
<color=red>and without a name... your a nobody</color>
<color=red>or atleast a nobody in their world</color>
<color=red>and being a nobody in their world... </color>
<color=red>I'd take a black hole over the sea</color>
<<set $quest to "Return to Co-Worker scrubs">>
===



title: transmition3
---
<color=red>okay, okay, you win. </color>
<color=red>I'm beat, really. You can walk out of here if you want </color>
<color=red>but at least hear my pitch okay? </color>
<color=red>I haven't been rambling in your ear for nothing </color>
<color=red>so, here goes </color>
<color=red>that core is worthless...</color>
<color=red>or, at least to Aquilla</color>
<color=red>come on, ever since they bought out rights to all fabricator technology these batteries are cheaper to make than Synthmeat</color>
<color=red>it's getting recycled or maybe even trashed the second you turn it in</color>
<color=red>but for us, people on the edge, that battery could help us thrive out</color>
<color=red>and maybe even make something of a life out here, one worth living</color>
<color=red>away from Aquilla, the only place in the whole system that they don't own. </color>
<color=red>a place where you can exist away from their watchfull eye </color>
<color=red>a field where you can work for yourself, not a tyrant in a rocking chair </color>
<color=red>see, thay hate that</color>
<color=red>they REALLY hate that </color>
<color=red>they want to control everyone, everything</color>
<color=red>they want to dictate humanity's evolution, make it revolve around them </color>
<color=red>they want everything to opperate they way they envision</color>
<color=red>in their picture </color>
<color=red>eveything out the picture, obscure, fed to the sea </color>
<color=red>you weren't sent to retreive property</color>
<color=red>you were sent to keep it out of our hands</color>
<color=red>to keep us obscure</color>
<color=red>to hold us down, without a chance of ever becoming something of ourselves</color>
<color=red>something other than their vision </color>
<color=red>your a dam, keeping the ocean at bay </color>
<color=red>because if word of actual settelments beyond Aquilla space starts coming out</color>
<color=red>the the vision will be ruined</color>
<color=red>the ocean would leak through the picture frame</color>
<color=red>Aquilla would no longer be a constant that is the only thing we can live under</color>
<color=red>people would have choice </color>
<color=red>have you taken in where you are?</color>
<color=red>some would kill for this oppertunity</color>
<color=red>the strings are loose, extractor, looser than they ever have been</color>
<color=red>take them off</color>
<color=red>dissapear into the edge</color>
<color=red>join us</color>
<color=red>we've got technicians that can disable tracking from your chip</color>
<color=red>not that it would matter, to Aquilla it's just another pawn lost to sea</color>
<color=red>but to you, the discovery of freedom</color>
<color=red>a new life, under no one </color>
<color=red>a chance to act on your own </color>
<color=red>this can be the beggining of your story</color>
<color=red>the story you can write</color>
<color=red>we're in one of the docking bays, waiting for you. </color>
<color=red>if you take the right door, then that story ends, and you return back to you old life, into the ceartainty within the picture frames</color>
<color=red>but if you take the left door</color>
<color=red>then I can show you just how deep the sea goes</color>
<color=red>and the light at the end of it</color>
<<set $quest to "Make a choice">>
===


